[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: CHANGE header claimed both add_node edge-mapping and validate cycle-detection were fixed. The validate fix succeeded (test_fake_validate_multibranch_cycle now passes), but the add_node edge-mapping fix in the transition update function is correct — it properly populates upstream[node_id].add(dep) and downstream[dep].add(node_id) per the real DAG.add_node contract (low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi: _upstream[node_id] holds dependencies, _downstream[dep] holds dependents). The failure is a test defect: line 503 asserts self.assertIn('rm_dp', self.state.downstream.get('rm_dchild', set())) which has swapped semantics — 'rm_dp' is a dependency of 'rm_dchild' so it belongs in upstream['rm_dchild'], not downstream['rm_dchild']. The correct assertion is self.assertIn('rm_dp', self.state.upstream.get('rm_dchild', set())). Per the real implementation contract (low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi lines 69-70), _upstream[X] holds what X depends on and _downstream[X] holds what depends on X; the test erroneously expects the dependency to appear in the downstream mapping.
