[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: CHANGE header fixed line 503 downstream→upstream swap but left remove_node transition update broken. The remove_node transition (lines 160-161) contains two generator expressions whose discard side-effects are never consumed: (self.state.upstream.get(dep, set()).discard(node_id) for dep in self.state.nodes) and (self.state.downstream.get(dep, set()).discard(node_id) for dep in self.state.nodes). Being tuple elements of a lazy-expression chain, they are never iterated, so upstream and downstream entries for dependents/dependees are never cleaned up. Per the DAG contract (low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi), remove_node must remove the node's upstream/downstream edges from all dependent nodes. Fix: replace the two generator expressions with consumed for-loops that call self.state.upstream[dep].discard(node_id) and self.state.downstream[dep].discard(node_id) for each dep in self.state.nodes.
